  if v_s2 = 'old' then
    update public.academy_capstones
       set prompt = 'Six numbers, at a mud density of 1500 kg/m3 rather than the 1440 the lessons run on. Fields 1 and 2 use the HORIZONTAL well''s DRILL PIPE, the third string component at 0.127 m outside and 0.1086104 m inside diameter and 33.126528414 kg/m, in the OPEN hole at 0.2159 m diameter (not the 0.2204974 m casing) at an inclination of 90 degrees. Report: (1) that pipe''s SINUSOIDAL buckling limit; (2) its HELICAL buckling limit, which is the first times a constant that is not 2; (3) the MAXIMUM TORSION utilization over the horizontal well''s profile while rotating on bottom at the book friction factors, which is not the tension utilization; (4) the total SLIDING DISTANCE for a rotating schedule of 30 hours at 150 rpm followed by 20 hours at 90 rpm, which needs no torque and drag run at all; (5) the WORST CASING WEAR DEPTH in millimetres from that schedule on those side forces, at a wear factor of 2 mm3/kN.m in 30 m intervals; and (6) the worst WALL LOSS as a percentage from the same run. Type 1500 into the buckling and wear explorer''s mud density box: field 3 is its What the pipe has left view, and fields 5 and 6 are its casing wear view with the two schedule entries typed into its rows.'
